### Suggested independent additions (not implemented by this document)

**Paid order count** — example assuming each order has one row in `fact_order_process`:

```dax
Paid Orders =
CALCULATE(
    DISTINCTCOUNT(fact_order_process[order_id]),
    NOT ISBLANK(fact_order_process[pay_date])
)
```

**Unpaid order count** — counts orders without a recorded payment date, *which may also mean missing data*:

```dax
Orders Without Payment Date =
CALCULATE(
    DISTINCTCOUNT(fact_order_process[order_id]),
    ISBLANK(fact_order_process[pay_date])
)
```

**Average order-to-payment days** — example using date subtraction and excluding unmatched payment dates:

```dax
Avg Days to Payment =
AVERAGEX(
    FILTER(
        fact_order_process,
        NOT ISBLANK(fact_order_process[order_date]) &&
        NOT ISBLANK(fact_order_process[pay_date]) &&
        fact_order_process[pay_date] >= fact_order_process[order_date]
    ),
    DATEDIFF(
        fact_order_process[order_date],
        fact_order_process[pay_date],
        DAY
    )
)
```

These are **templates**, not verified existing measures. Adapt to the real grain, date types, filters, and business definition. For example, a missing payment date does not automatically mean the invoice is overdue.

